# Build context hygiene + safety. The image is built from the REPO ROOT
# (docker build -f agent-worker/Dockerfile .), so without this the whole
# checkout — including data/ (API keys and password hashes in plaintext JSON),
# .env and the LiveKit keypair — is shipped to the Docker daemon on every
# build. The Dockerfile's COPYs are selective, so nothing here reaches the
# image today; this keeps it that way if a COPY is ever broadened, and stops a
# multi-hundred-MB .venv/.git from crawling into the context. Anything the
# Dockerfile actually COPYs (agent-worker/, web-widget/, assets/) is NOT listed.

# --- operator secrets: must never enter a build context --------------------
data/
.env
*.env
!.env.example
livekit.yaml
# persona-voices.json is operator-local and names their personas/voice samples.
# The image ships persona-voices.example.json and falls back to it; a local
# build must not bake the operator's real map into a published layer.
agent-worker/persona-voices.json

# --- version control + local environments ----------------------------------
.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
bin/

# --- caches and build junk -------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
*.log

# --- not part of the runtime image -----------------------------------------
# Dev harnesses, working notes, upstream reference copies, design bundles.
tools/
subwave-probe/
subwave-openapi.json
notes-archive/
chromeprofile*/
*.zip
.claude/
